EO:13058,FRDOC:00-7209,00-7209,Proposed Rule,2000-03-23,65 FR 15592,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2000/03/23/00-7209.txt,c6caa705c2161db87bfd22a94f441754512015870de567ec7591a1433d676ccd,"This policy is based on Executive Order 13058 that prohibits, with limited exceptions, smoking of tobacco products in all Federal buildings."
EO:13058,FRDOC:02-30050,02-30050,Rule,2002-12-13,67 FR 76820,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2002/12/13/02-30050.txt,658c1d8cdda87f2ec571f9ccbeb8f691130da3af715219bf1b28ce7f817841e6,"Pursuant to Executive Order 13058, ``Protecting Federal Employees and the Public From Exposure to Tobacco Smoke in the Federal Workplace'' (3 CFR, 1997 Comp., p. 216), it is the policy of the executive branch to establish a smoke-free environment for Federal employees and members of the public visiting or using Federal facilities."
EO:13058,FRDOC:05-21644,05-21644,Rule,2005-11-08,70 FR 67786,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2005/11/08/05-21644.txt,f199b70a929f4d466e188064744fabef8781e6691b2a9b2c9fc86bc93b9206d2,"Pursuant to Executive Order 13058, ``Protecting Federal Employees and the Public From Exposure to Tobacco Smoke in the Federal Workplace'' (3 CFR, 1997 Comp., p. 216), it is the policy of the Executive branch to establish a smoke-free environment for Federal employees and members of the public visiting or using Federal facilities."
EO:13058,FRDOC:2014-28620,2014-28620,Rule,2014-12-08,79 FR 72545,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,2,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2014/12/08/2014-28620.txt,c74765e9d41c9123e35ad2d215dd29a898195c2fe76f5cce52f3868b9369fe1e,"Comment: The rule is contrary to 5 U.S.C. 7301, E.O. 13058 (banning smoking of tobacco products in all federal buildings except--see sec. 2(b)), which says the order does not extend to residential accommodation for persons involuntarily residing in a federal government building."
EO:13058,FRDOC:2016-31957,2016-31957,Proposed Rule,2017-01-06,82 FR 1647,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2017/01/06/2016-31957.txt,886c8abe72d52d79f4706f7c34d4e0c57068df7d938879ec6dc4cd554aecbf9f,"The purpose of the Order--in conformity with Executive Order 13058 (Protecting Federal Employees and the Public From Exposure to Tobacco Smoke in the Federal Workplace)--is to ``protect employees and park visitors from the health hazards and annoyances associated with'' exposure to environmental tobacco smoke, commonly known as ``second-hand'' smoke, which is a known human carcinogen."
EO:13058,FRDOC:2024-31206,2024-31206,Proposed Rule,2025-01-15,90 FR 4398,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2025/01/15/2024-31206.txt,9e6465bd7ab4c09bb212546b33bd1fbc5c36e22688dc9ba14a8093062fb559d5,"Specifically, E.O. 13058, Protecting Federal Employees and the Public from Exposure to Tobacco Smoke in the Federal Workplace,\25\ establishes a smoke-free environment for federal employees and members of the public visiting or using Federal facilities by expressly prohibiting the smoking of tobacco products."
EO:13058,FRDOC:97-27703,97-27703,Notice,1997-10-20,62 FR 54461,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,3,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/1997/10/20/97-27703.txt,a0478312d6851b568393beff4a69730fc5a3982869191ca6aa0ea4155575d2cc,"On August 9, 1997, President Clinton signed Executive Order 13058, entitled ``Protecting Federal Employees and the Public From Exposure to Tobacco Smoke in the Federal Workplace,'' (62 FR 43451, August 13, 1997), to establish a smoke-free environment for Federal employees and members of the public visiting or using Federal facilities."
