EO:13099,FRDOC:E8-31131,E8-31131,Rule,2009-01-02,74 FR 9,cross_reference,mention,False,False,True,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2009/01/02/E8-31131.txt,14f5f8bbd96c51ad3f1318ba9626c9774aa4197030a6f9c563e07716d1f0d28d,"Some of these prohibitions can be found in Sections 2339A and 2339B of Title 18 of the United States Code, Executive Order 12947, as amended by Executive Order 13099, Executive Order 13224, and Title VIII of the USA Patriot Act. Accordingly, USAID's authority to conduct vetting is implied from these authorities since, to avoid violation of the authorities, USAID must use some sort of screening."
