EO:13659,FRDOC:2018-20205,2018-20205,Notice,2018-09-18,83 FR 47129,amendment,modifying,True,False,False,,2,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2018/09/18/2018-20205.txt,290720cc66031ec5dc53a59439967c08866e7f9c494bdbb77ac8e6d79c394a2e,"The FTR was amended on April 19, 2017, through the issuance of a Final Rule, ``Clarification on Filing Requirements,'' to make changes related to the implementation of the International Trade Data System (ITDS), in accordance with the Executive Order 13659, Streamlining the Export/Import Process for American Businesses."
EO:13659,FRDOC:2018-26538,2018-26538,Notice,2018-12-07,83 FR 63152,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,2,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2018/12/07/2018-26538.txt,31e3527987ec928f3cda4fc27aa7b623f368e27bfebbce268cbf8fa2fd4d9be3,"Additionally, the Census Bureau revised language in the FTR to reflect the implementation of the International Trade Data System, in accordance with the Executive Order 13659, Streamlining the Export/Import Process for America's Businesses."
EO:13659,FRDOC:2019-26452,2019-26452,Notice,2019-12-09,84 FR 67255,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2019/12/09/2019-26452.txt,d39f63c297e71cc2e5270000aa523c070feadec9d2ae45e68d5b77fb37386671,"In instances where the AES filing is not required, the proper exemption or exclusion legend must be noted on the commercial loading documents per Section 30.7 of the FTR. CBP is currently conducting pilots to test the functionality regarding the filing of export manifests for air, rail, and ocean cargo to the ACE. These pilots will further the CBP initiatives set forth in the SAFE Port Act of 2006"
EO:13659,FRDOC:2020-01984,2020-01984,Notice,2020-02-03,85 FR 5928,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/02/03/2020-01984.txt,9b7fa875992d96bdee7b621dd75cabaf481fef0481b50641c50dd86db6723d40,"APHIS intends to begin applying Harmonized Tariff Schedule flags, which will alert filers who opted to submit electronically using ACE. Full implementation of the message set will bring APHIS into compliance with the mandates of the Security and Accountability For Every Port Act of 2006 and Executive Order 13659."
EO:13659,FRDOC:2020-03895,2020-03895,Rule,2020-03-06,85 FR 12985,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/03/06/2020-03895.txt,2e4516c1f2a7a2f95e53e59fe97697be9d2a6f648793baff2f1f9147caf57228,This mandate was instituted through the Border Interagency Executive Council's (BIEC) effort to implement Executive Order 13659 and its governance structure to ensure coordination.
EO:13659,FRDOC:2020-05159,2020-05159,Proposed Rule,2020-03-16,85 FR 14810,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/03/16/2020-05159.txt,5887e2895347bef898d0a172b353eae24d8f51dab2bbd8c7bf4707926ee1dd53,"In support of the International Trade Data System (ITDS), as mandated by Executive Order 13659, the DCP has successfully implemented the online versions of its import and export applications for controlled substances and listed chemicals (DEA Form 161, 236, 357, and 486)."
EO:13659,FRDOC:2020-10581,2020-10581,Notice,2020-05-18,85 FR 29741,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/05/18/2020-10581.txt,ef57f23482130c1a202186ba06dcb484802d85ea9bb1140c476b7116fa20fd8b,"In compliance with Executive Order 13659, Streamlining the Export/ Import Process for America's Businesses (79 FR 10657, Feb. 25, 2014), ATF joined CBP's pilot test and encouraged voluntary participation of U.S. exporters of National Firearms Act (NFA) firearms, as defined under title 26, United States Code (U.S.C.), section 5845(a))."
EO:13659,FRDOC:2020-21289,2020-21289,Notice,2020-09-28,85 FR 60756,cross_reference,mention,False,False,False,,1,False,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2020/09/28/2020-21289.txt,4ca8b103f6c83b8b425ab0a48374536a363e5d065208863e9c476478cd1d963c,Full implementation of the message set will bring APHIS into compliance with the mandates of the Security and Accountability For Every Port Act of 2006 and Executive Order 13659.
