EO:13957,EO:14003,2021-01924,Presidential Document,2021-01-27,86 FR 7231,revocation,ending,True,False,False,True,3,True,https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/text/2021/01/27/2021-01924.txt,bc7e1a42e1aa7747f3e1e352a3d88e6a430ce4c87e40c2db8e3ff1e1de0943c2,"Revocation of Schedule F. (a) The creation of a new Schedule F excepted service category in Executive Order 13957 of October 21, 2020 (Creating Schedule F in the Excepted Service), not only was unnecessary to the conditions of good administration, but also undermined the foundations of the civil service and its merit system principles, which were essential to the Pendleton Civil Service Reform Act"
